/**
 * @addtogroup Foundation_BuildGuide_Arduino
 *
 * Foundation is designed to remain Arduino-compatible without modifying the
 * repository structure.
 *
 * Arduino requires:
 *
 * @code
 * library.properties
 * src/
 * examples/
 * @endcode
 *
 * Other directories such as docs, cmake, tests, scripts, and build support files
 * are ignored by the Arduino IDE.
 *
 * @section FoundationBuildArduinoSource Source Mode
 *
 * Arduino should normally use Foundation in source mode.
 *
 * @subsection FoundationBuildArduinoLanguage Language Level
 *
 * Stock Arduino cores compile sketches as C++11 (Arduino AVR Boards 1.8.x uses
 * avr-gcc 7.3.0 with `-std=gnu++11`), and a library cannot change that flag.
 * When `ARDUINO` is defined, Foundation therefore accepts C++11 instead of its
 * usual C++17 minimum, so the IDE works without editing the core. Below C++14,
 * mutators such as `Ratio::SetNumerator()` are ordinary inline functions rather
 * than `constexpr`; below C++17, the `_v` TypeTraits variables are not declared
 * (use `::value`). A core that already compiles as C++17 gets the full API.
 *
 * @subsection FoundationBuildArduinoIncludes Includes
 *
 * The Arduino builder discovers a library only through a header in its `src/`
 * root. Include `<Foundation.h>` (or a root module header such as
 * `<Foundation_Math.h>`) in the sketch before any nested header:
 *
 * @code{cpp}
 * #include <Foundation.h>
 * #include <Foundation/Math/Ratio.h>
 * @endcode
 *
 * A sketch that includes only `<Foundation/Math/Ratio.h>` fails with
 * `No such file or directory` because Foundation is never added to the include
 * path.
 *
 * @subsection FoundationBuildArduinoValidation Validation
 *
 * `scripts/test-arduino.sh`, or `scripts/test-arduino.ps1` on Windows,
 * compiles every sketch under `examples/Foundation`
 * for `arduino:avr:uno` from the repository's source layout with the
 * unmodified core flags, and fails on any warning in Foundation or its
 * examples because the core's `-fpermissive` otherwise hides type errors. It
 * is the Arduino source-mode gate; other boards and cores are not validated by
 * it.
 *
 * @section FoundationBuildArduinoMacros Macros
 *
 * Foundation modules may be selected using macros before includes.
 *
 * Example:
 *
 * @code{cpp}
 * #define FOUNDATION_FULL_BUILD
 * #include <Foundation.h>
 * @endcode
 *
 * @section FoundationBuildArduinoPrecompiled Precompiled Arduino Libraries
 *
 * Precompiled Arduino libraries are possible, but they are not universal.
 *
 * They must be separated by architecture and core, for example:
 *
 * @code
 * atmega328p_avrgcc_avr5
 * arduino_samd_cortex_m0plus
 * arduino_esp32_xtensa
 * @endcode
 *
 * Source mode is recommended for Arduino unless a very specific target is known.
 *
 * The `atmega328p_avrgcc_avr5` export is a CMake package and target archive. It
 * does not automatically create Arduino's architecture-specific precompiled
 * library directory layout or board metadata. To distribute it through Arduino,
 * verify the exact board core/toolchain version and package the archive according
 * to that core's library rules. Otherwise, keep using source mode so the Arduino
 * build compiles Foundation with the sketch's selected board flags.
 *
 * SAMD, ESP32, and other Arduino architectures require their own explicit
 * profiles; the ATmega328P AVR archive is not compatible with them.
 */
